+# v45 — preserve exact types while fixing audit-binder lint
+
+The v44 run passed all 21 established gates. The Amplification and ErrorScales
+modules built, but their exact-type audit invocations failed with ten unused
+hypothesis-name diagnostics. Three downstream gates were blocked. This is not
+an accepted five-gate error-layer result.
+
+## Changes
+
+Four audit files replace unused named proof binders with anonymous `_` binders.
+The hypotheses themselves are retained, including positivity, the nonnegative
+budget condition, the mass–budget gap, and all order/ratio conditions.
+
+| Audit | Unused proof names anonymized | Evidence |
+|---|---:|---|
+| EndpointAmplification | 7 | Reported in v44 |
+| EndpointErrorScales | 3 | Reported in v44 |
+| EndpointMomentTail | 9 | Same pattern in blocked source |
+| EndpointArithmeticRemainder | 3 | Same pattern in blocked source |
+
+All 31 expanded type/definition checks and 25 axiom targets in the error layer
+remain present. No theorem body, theorem statement, numerical constant, dependency
+pin, or gate changes. All 52 mathematical modules and the other 23 audit files
+are unchanged. Warning-as-error and the axiom allowlist remain enforced.
+
+The only runner change is the result prefix, now `erdos647_repo_v45_results_`.
+A version-label regression now checks consistency with the current status record
+instead of requiring an obsolete historical label. New targeted tests compare
+normalized expected types and catch this unused-binder pattern in audit source.
+They do not replace the actual Lean type/axiom gates.
+
+The completed mass–budget PR remains separate. This amplified-error PR still
+requires the full 26/26 gate result. Final same-scale endpoint absorption is
+subsequent work; no endpoint coefficient has yet been proved.
